                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "8bd1affe-2da7-36c4-9dc5-ed4e8ab5adb2",
                        "entry_id": "75acd287-6e77-31c1-b9e0-039c1d729006",
                        "glosses": [
                            "obdoba, analogon"
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "ef9bed41-dc55-408c-874b-df64e86843ce",
                                "sense_id": "8bd1affe-2da7-36c4-9dc5-ed4e8ab5adb2",
                                "text": "We constantly seek to find, in the Quality event, analogues to our previous experiences. If we didn't we'd be unable to act. We build up our language in terms of these analogues. We build up our whole culture in terms of these analogues."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "e631b187-dd9d-4a7a-b78f-ae1aa1316def",
                                "sense_id": "8bd1affe-2da7-36c4-9dc5-ed4e8ab5adb2",
                                "text": "Dardashti and his co-authors concentrate on a particular example (Example 17): ‘dumb holes’ and other analogues to gravitational black holes (Unruh 1981; Unruh 2008). Unlike real black holes, some of these analogues can be (and indeed have been) implemented and studied in the lab."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
